#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lp-goals — Lambdapi proof goals panel for Zed.

Zed extensions cannot open custom panels, so this tool provides the
goals view as a terminal app. It hooks onto the *same* Lambdapi LSP
session that Zed runs: the extension launches the server through
`lp-goals bridge`, a transparent stdio proxy that also exposes a Unix
socket. The panel subscribes there, so it sees exactly what Zed sees —
including unsaved buffer contents — without a second lambdapi process.

This script is embedded in the extension (via include_str!) and
materialized into the extension work dir when the language server
starts; the bridge then symlinks itself to ~/.local/bin/lp-goals so
the Zed tasks can invoke it (only when that directory already
exists; opt out with LAMBDAPI_NO_INSTALL). There is nothing to
install by hand — tools/lp-goals in the repo is the source of truth.

Usage:
    lp-goals serve [FILE]            Run the goals panel (persistent).
    lp-goals at FILE LINE [COL]      Send cursor position to the panel.
    lp-goals once FILE LINE [COL]    One-shot: print goals and exit.
    lp-goals bridge -- CMD ARG...    LSP proxy (launched by Zed).

LINE and COL are 1-based (as in Zed's $ZED_ROW / $ZED_COLUMN).

The panel attaches to a running bridge when it finds one, and falls
back to spawning its own `lambdapi lsp` (re-checking the file on save)
otherwise. `lp-goals at` talks to the panel over a second Unix socket
and exits immediately, so it can run as an invisible Zed task.

Follow mode (bridge only, on by default): the bridge diffs consecutive
buffer versions to infer the caret, so the panel tracks where you are
typing — proof goals update as you write tactics, no keypress needed.
It switches files automatically when you edit a different open .lp
buffer. In the terminal, single keys control the panel:
    f  toggle follow (pinned ↔ follow)   l  toggle logs   q  quit
`lp-goals at` still pings any position for a one-off peek.

Environment:
    LAMBDAPI_PATH        lambdapi binary (default: `which lambdapi`)
    LAMBDAPI_LIB_ROOT    lib root prefix (default: $OPAM_SWITCH_PREFIX)
    LAMBDAPI_MAP_DIRS    comma-separated MOD:DIR --map-dir overrides
    LP_GOALS_SOCKET      panel socket override (default: per-user dir)
    LP_BRIDGE_SOCKET     bridge socket override
    LAMBDAPI_NO_INSTALL  don't link lp-goals into ~/.local/bin
    NO_COLOR             disable ANSI colors
"""

